nning with only 2 cards. I must play conservatively and force them to use their cards. Playing ♠5 is the optimal move because it\'s my lowest card, forcing the landlord to either use a card to beat it or pass. This preserves my stronger cards (pairs and ♦2) to defend against whatever the landlord might play next. If I play a pair and the landlord doesn\'t have a higher pair, they might have two singles that could win the game on their next turns.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠5"]}'}
